.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt OPENWRT-ACL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openwrt-acl
.Nd manage the MAC accept-list of an OpenWrt SSID over ssh
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl f | Fl l
.Op Fl b Ar band
.Op Fl H Ar host
.Op Fl s Ar ssid
.Cm list | clients
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl f | Fl l
.Op Fl b Ar band
.Op Fl H Ar host
.Op Fl s Ar ssid
.Cm add | del
.Ar device ...
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows and changes the list of devices an OpenWrt router lets onto one
SSID, the MAC filter of each wireless interface carrying it.
It runs a small helper on the router through
.Xr ssh 1 ,
which reads and writes the list with
.Xr uci 1
and asks
.Xr ubus 1 ,
.Xr jsonfilter 1
and
.Xr iw 8
there; nothing beyond
.Xr ssh 1
is needed here.
.Pp
The radios carrying an SSID keep separate accept-lists, and the
difference between them means something: a device absent from the 5 GHz
list is confined to 2.4 GHz.
.Cm add
and
.Cm del
therefore act on every band, unless
.Fl b
names one.
.Pp
A device is named by its MAC address, as
.Ql aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff ,
.Ql AA-BB-CC-DD-EE-FF
or
.Ql aabbccddeeff ,
or by a name from
.Pa /etc/ethers
on the router, which is also where
.Cm list
and
.Cm clients
take the names they show.
A MAC matches an entry however it is stored: upper or lower case, with
colons, dashes, dots or none.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "clients"
.It Cm list
A table of every MAC on the accept-lists, with its name and a column
per radio, marked
.Ql confined
when some radio lacks it.
.It Cm clients
The stations associated with each radio, with their names.
.It Cm add Ar device ...
Add the devices to the accept-list of every radio carrying the SSID,
where they are not on it already.
.It Cm del Ar device ...
Remove the devices from every radio carrying the SSID.
.El
.Pp
A change is committed to
.Xr uci 1
first, which is the source of truth, and then applied.
Applying it costs a reassociation: hostapd reads its accept-list only
when its configuration is loaded, so the BSSes carrying the SSID are
reloaded, two seconds after the command returns, and their clients
reconnect within a few seconds.
The radio's other SSIDs are left alone unless
.Fl f
is given; where a BSS cannot be reloaded alone, because hostapd keeps
no accept-list file for it, the change waits for the next reload
instead.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-H host"
.It Fl b Ar band
Act on the radios of one band only:
.Ql 2.4 ,
.Ql 5
or
.Ql 6
.Po also
.Ql 2.4GHz
or
.Ql 2g ,
and so on
.Pc ,
or
.Ql all ,
the default.
.It Fl f
Apply a change with a full
.Ql wifi reload ,
which drops every client of every SSID, rather than reloading only the
BSSes carrying this one.
.It Fl H Ar host
The router, as an
.Xr ssh 1
destination; the default is
.Ev OPENWRT_ACL_HOST .
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl l
Commit a change to
.Xr uci 1
without applying it: it takes effect at the next reload, disturbing
nobody now.
.It Fl n
A dry run: show the plan of changes, one
.Ql + section mac
or
.Ql - section mac
line each, and change nothing.
.It Fl s Ar ssid
The SSID to act on, matched whole; the default is
.Ev OPENWRT_ACL_SSID .
.El
.Pp
.Fl f
and
.Fl l
exclude one another.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width OPENWRT_ACL_HOST
.It Ev OPENWRT_ACL_HOST
The router, when
.Fl H
is not given; the default is
.Ql maxwell .
.It Ev OPENWRT_ACL_SSID
The SSID, when
.Fl s
is not given; the default is
.Ql rezo_zero .
.El
.Sh FILES
On the router:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/ethers
The names of devices, one
.Ql mac name
line each; dnsmasq reads it too.
.It Pa /var/run/hostapd- Ns Ar ifname Ns Pa .maclist
hostapd's accept-list for one interface, rewritten before its BSS is
reloaded.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success; and, for
.Cm list
and
.Cm clients ,
also a failure on the router
.Pq Sx CAVEATS .
.It 1
A failure on the router: no wireless interface carries the SSID, a
name is not in its
.Pa /etc/ethers ,
or a change could not be made.
.It 255
.Xr ssh 1
could not reach the router, for
.Cm add
and
.Cm del .
.It 2
A command line that cannot be right: an unknown command, a device
that is neither a MAC address nor a name,
.Fl f
with
.Fl l .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Which devices may join, and on which bands:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ openwrt-acl list
.Ed
.Pp
Let a phone onto the 2.4 GHz radio only, after seeing the plan:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ openwrt-acl -n -b 2.4 add aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:01
$ openwrt-acl -b 2.4 add aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:01
.Ed
.Pp
Remove a device named in
.Pa /etc/ethers ,
for the next reload:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ openwrt-acl -l del laptop
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr ethers 5 ,
.Xr iw 8
.Sh CAVEATS
The defaults, the router
.Ql maxwell
and the SSID
.Ql rezo_zero ,
are the author's; set
.Ev OPENWRT_ACL_HOST
and
.Ev OPENWRT_ACL_SSID ,
or use
.Fl H
and
.Fl s .
.Pp
The update is not live: installing hostapd-utils on the router would
allow one,
.Ql hostapd_cli accept_acl add_mac ,
which
.Nm
does not use.
.Pp
The status of
.Cm list
and
.Cm clients
is that of the table they print: a failure on the router is reported
on stderr, but the exit status is 0.
